This improves DX by removing a need for a user to remember to add a trailing slash at the end of the custom URL used by `haveIBeenPwned.ts`:

```diff
const matcherPwned = matcherPwnedFactory(fetch, zxcvbnOptions, {
-  url: "/api/pwnedpasswords/"
+  url: "/api/pwnedpasswords"
});
```

Set correct tile sizes on root ops instead of using the same tile sizes as the following pack ops.

Currently to set the tile sizes for pack ops, we first use `adjustTileSizesForPackOp` to scale down the tile sizes on the root op according the the inner tile sizes then call `setLoweringConfigForComputeOps` to copy the scaled tile size to the pack op.

This results in misleading lowering config on the root op because its actual tile sizes is scaled up from the pack op later in the tile-and-fuse.

So instead of scaling down the tile sizes on root op, this change aligns the tile sizes on the root op to inner tile size, then scale down the sizes when we copy them to the pack op. This way it keeps lower configs on both root and pack op accurate.

Here is an example after this change. We can see that the lowering config on the generic op is set to `[[64, 64], [16, 16]]` (previous it would be `[4, 64], [1, 16]`). This correctly reflects the actual tiling size when it is tiled-and-fused with the pack op.

